# Astra browser layer — product metadata and services.
#
# This layer owns Astra-specific state that Chromium does not own:
#   - AstraWorkspaceService      (spaces/workspace metadata)
#   - AstraFavoriteService       (favorite folder metadata)
#   - AstraTabFeatures           (per-tab Astra metadata, via WebContentsUserData)
#   - AstraTabRulesService       (auto-action rules for tabs)
#   - AstraSessionRestoreHelper  (bridge between Chromium session service and
#                                 Astra tab metadata)
#   - astra_session_metadata     (serialization helpers for Astra session data)
#   - AstraCommandDelegate       (Astra-only command dispatch)
#   - astra_prefs                (shared pref key registration + defaults)
#
# Rules:
#   - Reuse Chromium for Profile, WebContents, TabStripModel,
#     NavigationController, history, downloads, permissions, passwords,
#     extensions, DevTools, WebUI, update, and policy.
#   - Use ProfileKeyedService for profile-scoped metadata.
#   - Use content::WebContentsUserData for tab-scoped metadata.
#   - Never declare a service that duplicates a Chromium-owned service.
#   - All persistence goes through Chromium PrefService — no custom file I/O.
#   - Session restore is owned by Chromium; Astra only adds metadata.

